     ccrroonn is a daemon that runs commands at preset times.  It
     takes no command-line arguments; it is normally started
     once, from /eettcc/rrcc, and never exits.

     After starting, ccrroonn sets its user and group ids to those of
     ddaaeemmoonn (if that user is found in the password file), changes
     its working directory to /bbiinn, and enters a loop that wakes
     once every minute.  Each time it wakes, it reopens
     /uussrr/lliibb/ccrroonnttaabb and reads it one entry at a time, comparing
     the entry's time fields against the current time.

